    {
      "id": 10,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "About this dashboard — model, targets & references",
      "gridPos": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": 28,
        "w": 24,
        "h": 13
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## How to read this board\n\n**Goal:** predict *when* a specific campsite/date sells out. With little history those predictions are not trustworthy yet — the **readiness gauge** above is the honest gate, and model ETAs stay hidden until it clears.\n\n### The model (robot-geographical-society PREDICT.md)\nSell-out is a **time-to-event / survival** problem on the daily `sites/` snapshots:\n\n- **C0** — build per-(site, date) at-risk intervals from the snapshots.\n- **C1** — Kaplan–Meier survival curves per cohort (day-of-week × season × popularity).\n- **C2** — discrete-time **logistic hazard** → survival curve → median sell-out ETA + risk band.\n- **Expected-accuracy boundary** — best achievable AUC given history so far, 0.5 + 0.34·(1 − e^(−months/3)), rising toward a **~0.84** ceiling (one sample per annual peak).\n\n### Targets — what *ready* means\n`readiness = (event_score · coverage · depth_score)^(1/3)` — a geometric mean, so the weakest component holds the gauge down.\n\n| Component | Target | Meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| events | **500** sell-outs | enough events to fit a stable hazard model |\n| coverage | **100%** | cells with ≥2 snapshots (an at-risk interval exists) |\n| depth | **6** intervals/cell | burn-down resolution per cell |\n\nBands: red **< 0.33** hide · amber **0.33–0.80** low-confidence · green **≥ 0.80** show ETAs.\n\n### Your data\nThe stat row and gauges above are recomputed every run from the R2 `sites/` history — campgrounds tracked, collection days, total (site, date) cells, sell-outs observed, coverage, median depth, and the current expected-accuracy boundary. Early on the bottleneck is **depth & coverage**, not events: most cells have only one snapshot so far, so few at-risk intervals exist. The gauge climbs as the daily collector revisits each site over the coming weeks; the countdown above estimates how long until the expected-accuracy boundary reaches a usable ~0.80 AUC.\n\n### References\n\n- Design & checkpoints — **PREDICT.md** · rgs PR [#71](https://github.com/tommyroar/robot-geographical-society/pull/71)\n- Readiness + accuracy formulas — [predict/readiness.py](https://github.com/tommyroar/robot-geographical-society/blob/feat/predict-plan/predict/readiness.py), mirrored in `campsites/ingest.py`\n- Upstream data — [recreation.gov](https://www.recreation.gov) · [WA goingtocamp](https://washington.goingtocamp.com)\n- Methods — [Kaplan–Meier estimator](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaplan%E2%80%93Meier_estimator) · [survival analysis](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Survival_analysis) · [Brier score](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brier_score)"
      }
    },
